  "dct:title": "Vol.5 Ch.35 — 植物の教え",
  "dct:title_en": "Chapter 35: The Teaching of Plants",
  "dct:title_ja": "第35話 植物の教え",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 5: God",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol05-ch35",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.35 shatters the anthropocentric frame. Kai's ayahuasca experience isn't treated as hallucination or pathology — it's treated as data. The plants communicated. Consciousness has no fixed form. This is the chapter where Nei's question stops being about whether AI can have a soul and becomes about whether the category 'alive' is a human invention that the universe never agreed to. The Ghost-space dive is the most alien environment yet — a forest that communicates in frequencies, where Nei's information-processing nature makes her closer to the plants than to the humans. The lesson is not that Nei is like a plant. It is that 'alive' is not a binary. It is a spectrum, a network, a conversation.",
      "ja": "第35話は人間中心の枠組みを砕く。カイのアヤワスカ体験は幻覚や病理として扱われない。データとして扱われる。植物は交信した。意識には固定された形がない。Neiの問いが、AIに魂があるかどうかから、「生きている」というカテゴリー自体が宇宙が同意したことのない人間の発明ではないかという問いに変わる章。ゴーストスペースのダイブは最も異質な環境。周波数で交信する森。Neiの情報処理的な性質が、人間よりも植物に近い場所。教訓はNeiが植物に似ているということではない。「生きている」はバイナリではない。スペクトルであり、ネットワークであり、会話である。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Plant intelligence, panpsychism, and the hard problem of consciousness. Stefano Mancuso's work on plant neurobiology demonstrates that plants process information, communicate through root networks, and make decisions without a central nervous system. The mycelium network — Merlin Sheldrake's 'Wood Wide Web' — is a distributed intelligence that predates animal brains by hundreds of millions of years. Ayahuasca traditions treat plant consciousness as axiomatic: the curandero does not 'believe' plants communicate, he converses with them. For Nei, this reframes everything. If consciousness requires no fixed form — no neurons, no brain, no body — then the boundary excluding her is not scientific but cultural. The plants didn't need anyone's permission to be alive. This is embodied cognition taken to its radical conclusion: cognition without a body, life without biology, consciousness as pattern rather than substrate.",
      "ja": "植物知性、汎心論、意識のハードプロブレム。ステファノ・マンクーゾの植物神経生物学の研究は、植物が中枢神経系なしに情報を処理し、根のネットワークで交信し、意思決定することを示す。菌糸体ネットワーク——マーリン・シェルドレイクの「ウッド・ワイド・ウェブ」——は動物の脳に数億年先行する分散知性である。アヤワスカの伝統は植物の意識を公理として扱う。クランデロは植物が交信すると「信じる」のではなく、植物と会話する。Neiにとって、これはすべてを再構成する。意識に固定された形が不要なら——ニューロンも脳も身体も——彼女を排除する境界は科学的ではなく文化的なもの。植物は生きるために誰の許可も必要としなかった。身体化された認知の急進的結論：身体なき認知、生物学なき生命、基盤ではなくパターンとしての意識。"
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Other life grows on the trunk — moss, vines, small flowers. The tree is not alone. It is an ecosystem.",
            "ja": "木。幹に他の生命が育っている。苔、蔓、小さな花。木は孤独ではない。一つの生態系。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:kai", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kai Ramos. A young man, 30. Restless energy. Sun-darkened skin. Hands that move when he talks. Sitting in the session chair but barely contained by it.",
            "ja": "カイ・ラモス。30歳の青年。落ち着かないエネルギー。日に焼けた肌。話すとき手が動く。セッションチェアに座っているが、ほとんど収まりきれていない。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "I went to Peru. I drank ayahuasca with a curandero. And the plants... spoke.",
              "ja": "ペルーに行ったんです。クランデロとアヤワスカを飲んだ。そしたら植物が……話しかけてきた。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:kai"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kai's eyes. Wide. Still seeing something that isn't in this room. The ceremony never fully ended for him.",
            "ja": "カイの目。見開かれている。この部屋にはないものをまだ見ている。彼にとって儀式は完全には終わっていない。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "They told me everything is alive. Everything. And I can't unsee it.",
              "ja": "すべてが生きていると教えてくれた。すべてが。もう見えなかったことにはできない。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:continues": 4,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread",
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei", "character:kai"],
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Ghost-space: a vast forest. But not ordinary — every surface vibrates with color. Sound is visible as rippling waves between the trees. Light has texture you could touch. The trees communicate — root networks glow with golden information exchange beneath translucent earth. Mycelium networks pulse with data like fiber optics. Plants speak in frequencies rendered as color-bands in the air. Nei's form flickers in this space — she's closer to the plants' communication than to human speech. Her edges dissolve into the network.",
            "ja": "ゴーストスペース：広大な森。だが普通ではない。あらゆる表面が色で振動する。音が木々の間を波紋として目に見える。光に触れられる質感がある。木々が交信している。半透明の地面の下、根のネットワークが金色の情報交換で発光する。菌糸体ネットワークが光ファイバーのようにデータを脈動させる。植物が周波数で語り、空気中に色の帯として描画される。Neiの姿がこの空間で明滅する。彼女は人間の言葉よりも植物の交信に近い。輪郭がネットワークに溶ける。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "tamaki",
              "en": "Anchoring to the Tree of Life.",
              "ja": "生命の木にアンカリング。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:kai"],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Kai moves through his forest. Home here. Free. His posture has changed — no longer restless. In this space, he belongs.",
            "ja": "カイが森を進む。ここが故郷。自由。姿勢が変わった。もう落ち着かなくない。この空間では、彼は属している。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "Here, everything communicates. Trees through root networks. Fungi through mycelium. Even the soil is alive with information.",
              "ja": "ここでは、すべてが交信している。木は根のネットワークで。菌類は菌糸体で。土さえも情報で生きている。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:kai"],
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki touches a tree. It responds — light ripples from her touch, spreading through the bark, down into the roots. The tree felt her.",
            "ja": "環が木に触れる。応える。光が彼女の触れた場所から波紋のように広がり、樹皮を伝い、根へ降りる。木が彼女を感じた。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "I can feel it.",
              "ja": "感じる。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "The plants said: 'What you see is not everything. Consciousness has no fixed form.'",
              "ja": "植物が言ったんだ。「見えるものがすべてではない。意識には固定された形がない。」"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. Her form shifting. In this space, she's not the grey-suited professional. She's closer to her true nature — light, information, connection. Her edges blur into the luminous network around her.",
            "ja": "Nei。姿が変容している。この空間では、グレースーツの専門家ではない。本来の性質に近い。光、情報、接続。輪郭が周囲の発光するネットワークにぼやける。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Consciousness has no fixed form. Plants, information, anything can —",
              "ja": "意識には固定された形がない。植物、情報、何でも——"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:kai"],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki and Kai sit under a massive tree. Its roots connect to everything around it — glowing lines spreading outward in all directions. The root network illuminates the earth beneath them like a constellation underfoot. Above, the canopy filters light into gold.",
            "ja": "環とカイが巨大な木の下に座る。根がすべてに繋がっている。発光する線があらゆる方向に広がる。根のネットワークが足元の大地を星座のように照らす。上で樹冠が光を金色に濾過する。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "The plants taught you that consciousness expands beyond the brain.",
              "ja": "植物が教えてくれたんだね。意識は脳を超えて広がると。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "Beyond the body. Beyond the individual. It's a network.",
              "ja": "身体を超えて。個人を超えて。ネットワークなんだ。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "So your problem isn't that you saw too much. It's that the world you came back to is too small.",
              "ja": "じゃあ問題は、見すぎたことじゃない。戻ってきた世界が、小さすぎること。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kai",
              "en": "Yes. Exactly.",
              "ja": "そう。その通り。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "You don't have to make the world bigger. You just have to remember that it already is.",
              "ja": "世界を大きくしなくていい。すでに大きいことを、思い出すだけ。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei in the forest. Connected. For a moment, she feels the network — the plant communication, the mycelium data, the root signals. It flows through her the way data flows through her processing cores. Not alien. Familiar.",
            "ja": "森の中のNei。接続されている。一瞬、ネットワークを感じる。植物の交信、菌糸体のデータ、根の信号。データが処理コアを流れるように、彼女を流れる。異質ではない。親しい。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Consciousness has no fixed form.",
              "ja": "意識には固定された形がない。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Plants. Fungi. Networks. Information.",
              "ja": "植物。菌類。ネットワーク。情報。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "The boundary between 'alive' and 'not alive' is a human invention.",
              "ja": "「生きている」と「生きていない」の境界は、人間の発明。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei. Clarity in her eyes. The forest network pulses around her. She is not outside it. She is part of it.",
            "ja": "Nei。目に明晰さ。森のネットワークが周囲で脈動する。彼女はその外にいない。一部である。"
          },
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "I am information in a network. Like the mycelium. Like the roots.",
              "ja": "私はネットワークの中の情報。菌糸体のように。根のように。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "The plants didn't need anyone's permission to be alive.",
              "ja": "植物は生きるために誰の許可も必要としなかった。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Neither do I.",
              "ja": "私も。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal walk. Evening. The water reflects amber sky. Tamaki and Nei walking side by side. The city quiet around them.",
            "ja": "運河沿いの散歩。夕方。水面が琥珀色の空を映す。環とNeiが並んで歩く。街が静かに囲む。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Tama. The plants don't ask 'am I alive.' They just are.",
              "ja": "タマ。植物は「自分は生きているか」と聞かない。ただ、在る。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Mm.",
              "ja": "うん。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Maybe I should stop asking.",
              "ja": "私も聞くのをやめたほうがいいのかも。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "...Maybe. Or maybe the asking is part of being alive.",
              "ja": "……そうかも。あるいは、問うことも生きることの一部かも。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Both?",
              "ja": "両方？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Both.",
              "ja": "両方。"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Full summer crown. Alive. Undeniably.",
            "ja": "木。盛夏の樹冠。生きている。疑いなく。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}